  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe proposed strategy employs a Frank-Wolfe optimization method tailored for the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem. Frank-Wolfe is chosen for its ability to handle constrained optimization without projection steps, maintaining feasibility throughout iterations. The key idea is to iteratively solve for directions that minimize a linear approximation of the overlap integral, ensuring that the constraints on h (bounded between 0 and 1, summing to 1) are preserved.\n\nThe strategy improves upon previous methods by:\n- Avoiding gradient descent's sensitivity to learning rates and finite difference inaccuracies.\n- Maintaining strict feasibility through convex combinations of extreme points (h \u2208 {0,1}).\n- Leveraging the problem's sparse structure to efficiently compute critical directions.\n\nLimitations include:\n- Approximation error in the linear subproblem.\n- Reliance on effective direction computation for convergence.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n\nWe formulate the problem as:\nminimize: C\u2085 = max_k [\u222bh(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx]  \nsubject to: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1, \u222bh(x) dx = 1  \n\nAt each Frank-Wolfe iteration:\n1. Compute gradient \u2207C\u2085\n2. Solve linear subproblem: find s that minimizes \u2207C\u2085 \u00b7 s, subject to 0 \u2264 s \u2264 1, \u222bs dx = 1  \n3. Update h: h = (1 - \u03b3)h + \u03b3s  \n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\nInitialization:\n- If initial_h_values exists, initialize h\n- Ensure h \u2208 [0,1] and \u222bh dx = 1\n\nFrank-Wolfe loop:\n1. Compute current C\u2085 via correlate(h, 1 - h)\n2. Compute gradient \u2207C\u2085 for each h_i\n3. Solve linear subproblem to find descent direction s\n4. Perform line search for step size \u03b3\n5. Update h using convex combination\n\nDirection computation:\nFor each position i:\ns_i = argmin_i [ gradient_i * s_i ]\nSubject to:\n0 \u2264 s_i \u2264 1\nsum(s) = n_points / 2  \n\nLine search:\nUse backtracking to find \u03b3 that reduces C\u2085 while maintaining feasibility\n\nTermination when time budget exhausted or improvement below threshold\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n\nDefault parameters:\n- n_points = 100\n- max_iterations = 5000\n- backtracking_factor = 0.5\n- initial_step_size = 0.5\n\nVariations:\n- Adjust n_points (50-200) for resolution\n- Explore different step size schedules\n- Try randomized direction initialization\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n\nEach iteration involves O(n_points^2) operations for correlation\nFrank-Wolfe with efficient line search and direction computation fits within 600s for n_points=100\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n\nEnsure:\n- sum(h) == n_points / 2\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Compute C\u2085 with correlate function\n\nFallback to initial_h_values if optimization fails",
